<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kota Bharu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kota Bharu is a city near the mouth of the Kelantan river in north-eastern Peninsular Malaysia and the royal capital of the state of Kelantan. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Muhammad II made it the seat of government in the 19th century. On 8 December 1941 Japanese troops landed on the nearby beaches, shortly before the attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a>, opening the Malayan campaign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kota-bharu.jpg" alt="Kota Bharu" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CK Tan · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kelantan_Royal_Palace_Gate_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
